Subject: [PATCH 8/8] =?UTF-8?q?aarch64:=20init=20the=20PL011=20(RXE)=20on=20th?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20ACPI/SPCR=20serial=20path=20=E2=80=94=20fixes=20serial=20in?=
 =?UTF-8?q?put?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SPCR/ACPI serial path created the PL011 and enabled its IRQ but never
called SerialPort::init(), which is what sets the control register
(RXE | TXE | UARTEN). Without RXE the receiver is disabled, so serial *input*
never arrived under an ACPI boot -- only output worked, making the interactive
serial console (login getty) unusable. The device-tree path already calls
init(); this regressed for E-OS when R-401f let aarch64 boot under ACPI
(-machine virt) instead of forcing a device-tree boot (acpi=off). Call
init(false) in the SPCR path before storing COM1; enable_irq() still sets the
RX interrupt mask. Upstream-clean (the ACPI serial RX path is broken the same
way on mainline).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3c642030691238c62ef2141d2c5cd507c7b930ca)
---
 src/acpi/spcr.rs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/acpi/spcr.rs b/src/acpi/spcr.rs
index 5f55f1ed..8a564850 100644
--- a/src/acpi/spcr.rs
+++ b/src/acpi/spcr.rs
@@ -81,7 +81,14 @@ impl Spcr {
                                 PAGE_SIZE,
                             )
                         };
-                        let serial_port = uart_pl011::SerialPort::new(virt.data(), false);
+                        let mut serial_port = uart_pl011::SerialPort::new(virt.data(), false);
+                        // E-OS: the SPCR/ACPI path skipped init(), which sets the PL011
+                        // control register (RXE | TXE | UARTEN). Without RXE the receiver
+                        // is off, so serial *input* never arrives (only output worked) --
+                        // interactive serial login was impossible under an ACPI boot
+                        // (the device-tree path in dtb/serial.rs already calls init()).
+                        // enable_irq() below only sets the interrupt mask, not RXE.
+                        serial_port.init(false);
                         *COM1.lock() = SerialKind::Pl011(serial_port);
                         //TODO: enable IRQ on more platforms and interrupt types
                         if (spcr.interrupt_type & INTERRUPT_TYPE_GIC) == INTERRUPT_TYPE_GIC {
